From 71ec2f85ea62a0570870c780b9ea14963f15d0b9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: nyasha <nmushambi@proton.me>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 22:57:04 +1300
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: tegra132: flounder: do not invert the PMC interrupt
 polarity

The Palmas PMIC interrupt stormed (~1000 irq/s, the PMIC I2C bus ~10k
irq/s), starving every regulator operation: the tfa989x probe hung in
regulator_dev_lookup behind irq/72-palmas, the SDIO rescan blocked, and the
machine stalled in 'mode B'. The vendor DT has no nvidia,invert-interrupt
property in its PMC node; the port had added it. Without it the interrupt
counters stay quiet and snd-soc-tfa989x probes (both sound cards register).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/nvidia/tegra132-flounder.dts | 1 -
 1 file changed, 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/nvidia/tegra132-flounder.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/nvidia/tegra132-flounder.dts
index 30a362fd6..41470e8ad 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/nvidia/tegra132-flounder.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/nvidia/tegra132-flounder.dts
@@ -1163,7 +1163,6 @@ rt5677@0 {
 	};
 
 	pmc@7000e400 {
-		nvidia,invert-interrupt;
 		nvidia,suspend-mode = <0>;
 		nvidia,cpu-pwr-good-time = <500>;
 		nvidia,cpu-pwr-off-time = <300>;
-- 
2.56.0

